{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And Israel abode in Shittim, and the people began to commit harlotry.</b> Wherever וישב is written, punishment follows after it: ״וישב יעקב״ — ויבא יוסף את דבתם רעה, and he was sold. ״וישב יוסף במצרים״ — ויאמר יוסף אל אחיו הנה אנכי מת. ״וישב ישראל בארץ מצרים״ — and adjacent to it: ויקרבו ימי ישראל למות. ״וישב ישראל ויהודה בטח״ — and adjacent to it: ויקם ה' שטן לשלמה etc." "<b>In Shittim.</b> Rabbi Elazar says: Shittim is its name. And Rabbi Yehoshua says: they engaged in a matter of folly (shtut)." "<b>And the people began to commit harlotry.</b> They became profane (chulin) through harlotry, by the counsel of Balaam. And therefore he is punished with boiling semen, as is stated in tractate Gittin, chapter HaNezikin: measure for measure."], :book :numbers, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:10:13.926692713Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}